{
  "sutta_id": "SN11.5",
  "verses": [
    {
      "number": 1,
      "pali": "Linked Discourses 11.5",
      "english": "Linked Discourses 11.5"
    },
    {
      "number": 2,
      "pali": "Subhāsita-jaya Sutta",
      "english": "Victory Through What is Well Spoken"
    },
    {
      "number": 3,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "On one occasion the Blessed One was staying near Sāvatthī at Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. There he addressed the monks, “Monks!”"
    },
    {
      "number": 4,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "“Yes, lord,” the monks responded to him."
    },
    {
      "number": 5,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "The Blessed One said, “Once in the past the devas & asuras were arrayed for battle. Then Vepacitti the asura-king said to Sakka the deva-king: ‘Let there be victory through what is well spoken.’"
    },
    {
      "number": 6,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "“‘Yes, Vepacitti, let there be victory through what is well spoken.’"
    },
    {
      "number": 7,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "“So the devas & asuras appointed a panel of judges, (thinking,) ‘These will decide for us what is well spoken & poorly spoken.’"
    },
    {
      "number": 8,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "“Then Vepacitti the asura-king said to Sakka the deva-king, ‘Say a verse, deva-king!’"
    },
    {
      "number": 9,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "“When this was said, Sakka the deva-king said to Vepacitti the asura-king, ‘But you are the senior deity here, Vepacitti. You say a verse.’"
    },
    {
      "number": 10,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "“When this was said, Vepacitti recited this verse:"
    },
    {
      "number": 11,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "‘Fools would flare up even more"
    },
    {
      "number": 12,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "if there were no constraints."
    },
    {
      "number": 13,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "Thus an enlightened one"
    },
    {
      "number": 14,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "should restrain the fool"
    },
    {
      "number": 15,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "with a heavy stick.’"
    },
    {
      "number": 16,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "“When Vepacitti had said this verse, the asuras applauded but the devas were silent. So Vepacitti said to Sakka, ‘Say a verse, deva-king!’"
    },
    {
      "number": 17,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "“When this was said, Sakka recited this verse:"
    },
    {
      "number": 18,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "‘This, I think,"
    },
    {
      "number": 19,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "is the only constraint for a fool:"
    },
    {
      "number": 20,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "When, knowing the other’s provoked,"
    },
    {
      "number": 21,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "you mindfully grow calm.’"
    },
    {
      "number": 22,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "“When Sakka had said this verse, the devas applauded but the asuras were silent. So Sakka said to Vepacitti, ‘Say a verse, Vepacitti!’"
    },
    {
      "number": 23,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "“When this was said, Vepacitti recited this verse:"
    },
    {
      "number": 24,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "‘Vāsava , I see a fault"
    },
    {
      "number": 25,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "in this very forbearance:"
    },
    {
      "number": 26,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "When the fool thinks,"
    },
    {
      "number": 27,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "“He’s forbearing"
    },
    {
      "number": 28,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "out of fear of me,”"
    },
    {
      "number": 29,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "the idiot pursues you even more—"
    },
    {
      "number": 30,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "as a bull, someone who runs away.’"
    },
    {
      "number": 31,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "“When Vepacitti had said this verse, the asuras applauded but the devas were silent. So Vepacitti said to Sakka, ‘Say a verse, deva-king!’"
    },
    {
      "number": 32,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "“When this was said, Sakka recited this verse:"
    },
    {
      "number": 33,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "‘It doesn’t matter"
    },
    {
      "number": 34,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "whether he thinks,"
    },
    {
      "number": 35,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "“He’s forbearing"
    },
    {
      "number": 36,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "out of fear of me.”"
    },
    {
      "number": 37,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "One’s own true good"
    },
    {
      "number": 38,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "is the foremost good."
    },
    {
      "number": 39,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "Nothing better"
    },
    {
      "number": 40,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "than patience"
    },
    {
      "number": 41,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "is found."
    },
    {
      "number": 42,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "Whoever, when strong,"
    },
    {
      "number": 43,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "is forbearing"
    },
    {
      "number": 44,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "to one who is weak:"
    },
    {
      "number": 45,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "that’s the foremost patience."
    },
    {
      "number": 46,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "The weak must constantly endure."
    },
    {
      "number": 47,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "They call that strength"
    },
    {
      "number": 48,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "no strength at all:"
    },
    {
      "number": 49,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "whoever’s strength"
    },
    {
      "number": 50,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "is the strength of a fool."
    },
    {
      "number": 51,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "There’s no reproach"
    },
    {
      "number": 52,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "for one who is strong,"
    },
    {
      "number": 53,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "guarding—guarded by—Dhamma."
    },
    {
      "number": 54,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "You make things worse"
    },
    {
      "number": 55,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "when you flare up"
    },
    {
      "number": 56,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "at someone who’s angry."
    },
    {
      "number": 57,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "Whoever doesn’t flare up"
    },
    {
      "number": 58,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "at someone who’s angry"
    },
    {
      "number": 59,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "wins a battle"
    },
    {
      "number": 60,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "hard to win."
    },
    {
      "number": 61,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "You live for the good of both"
    },
    {
      "number": 62,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "—your own, the other’s—"
    },
    {
      "number": 63,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "when, knowing the other’s provoked,"
    },
    {
      "number": 64,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "you mindfully grow calm."
    },
    {
      "number": 65,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "When you work the cure of both"
    },
    {
      "number": 66,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "—your own, the other’s—"
    },
    {
      "number": 67,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "those who think you a fool"
    },
    {
      "number": 68,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "know nothing of Dhamma.’"
    },
    {
      "number": 69,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "“When Sakka had said this verse, the devas applauded but the asuras were silent. Then the deva & asura panel of judges said, ‘The verses said by Vepacitti the asura-king lie in the sphere of swords & weapons—thence arguments, quarrels, & strife. Whereas the verses said by Sakka the deva-king lie outside the sphere of swords & weapons—thence no arguments, no quarrels, no strife. The victory through what is well spoken goes to Sakka the deva-king.’"
    },
    {
      "number": 70,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "“And that, monks, is how the victory through what was well spoken went to Sakka the deva-king.”"
    }
  ]
}